text:
marta: Heads up — Acadia onboarding hit repeated 429s during our SDK preflight in their CI. They use the JS browser SDK with ephemeral token prefetch on deploys, and it looks like many runners try to refresh at the same time. Logs attached below.

alex: Can you paste the snippet? Is this during initial bootstrap or periodic refresh?

marta: Initial bootstrap + prefetch step we added to speed up cold starts. Snip from their CI logs:```
[INFO] prefetch: requesting ephemeral token
[WARN] 429 Too Many Requests - /v1/ephemeral_tokens (x10)
[DEBUG] retry in 100ms
[DEBUG] retry in 100ms
[ERROR] exhaustion after 5 retries
```

devon: Oof. Looks like a classic stampede — lots of parallel job runners all warming the token. Do they use our default prefetch config or custom?

marta: Default. They set "prefetch: true" and run 50 parallel CI jobs on deploy.

alex: Two quick mitigations: 1) suggest clients add jittered exponential backoff and per-process single-flight for token fetch; 2) server-side we can temporarily raise throttle window for Acadia while they ramp. Would CS like me to open a support whitelist for a 10min burst? :thinking: 

marta: Yes please. They'll be deploying today and want minimal failures. Can we also advise a client-side change for next deploy?

devon: Add this snippet to their SDK integration guide:```js
// simple single-flight + jittered backoff
let inflight = null;
async function getEphemeral() {
  if (inflight) return inflight;
  inflight = (async () => {
    for (let i=0;i<6;i++) {
      try {
        return await fetchToken();
      } catch (e) {
        await sleep(Math.floor(Math.random()*100) + Math.pow(2,i)*50);
      }
    }
    throw new Error('token fetch failed');
  })();
  try { return await inflight; } finally { inflight = null; }
}
```

marta: Perfect. I'll send that to Acadia.

ratebot: [alert] spike detected for tenant: acadia-corp — ephemeral_token request rate 12x baseline in last 2m. Auto-throttle triggered.

alex: I'll open a temporary burst exception ticket with infra — request: increase ephemeral_token rate by 5x for tenant acadia-corp for 15 minutes.

marta: ETA on ticket? They start rollout in ~25m.

alex: Filing now, pinging @infra. Ticket #BR-9123. If infra can't do 5x, ask for a short 10min window at current cap + guided retry is ok.

devon: Also recommend they set prefetch: "staggered" — use build id % numRunners to offset start times by up to 30s. That avoids a simultaneous spike.

marta: I'll include both code snippet and stagger suggestion in my message. I'll ask them to flip prefetch off if rollout fails and we'll re-run with smaller batch sizes.

ratebot: [update] BR-9123 created and assigned to infra-oncall.

alex: Follow-up: let's capture this as a CS playbook entry — "prefetch stampede during onboarding" with suggested customer-side hardening + when to request temporary burst. Marta, can you draft the short playbook after this thread?

marta: Yep, will draft and add to onboarding runbook. Will also collect their CI config and share post-mortem.

devon: One more note — we should consider adding a server-side guidance header (Retry-After with small randomized window) for ephemeral endpoints so SDKs can adopt deterministic behavior. Filing a follow-up RFC.

marta: Great. Thanks everyone — I'll update Acadia and circle back in ~1h with status. :thumbsup:
